# Slice 334 (Codex review of 333, item 1; the book, composition of the structural parts): merge composes the
# corresponding Structure parts of any operands by the same rules and the one map -- here two ordinary Structures with
# a nested part P, the second giving P a new field v: R's P holds u (from A) and v (from B), R's x is A's. A and B stay
# as written.
A:
    int: x 1
    P:
        int: u 2
    end: P
end: A
B:
    P:
        int: v 3
    end: P
end: B
R: merge(A; B)
int: u R\P\u
int: v R\P\v
int: x R\x
